(optical counter results)\n\n---\n\n## Article Metadata Features\n\n### Automatic Calculations\n\nWhen you publish an article, the system automatically:\n\n- **Reading time:** Calculates from word count (÷200 words/min)\n- **Word count:** Counts words in body text\n- **SEO metadata:** Generates from title + description\n- **Semantic density display:** Shows in article header (1-10)\n- **Related articles:** Lists links to related-articles slugs\n- **Tags display:** Renders as clickable tags (filtered links)\n\n### Sorting & Filtering\n\n**/blog?category=installation**\n- Lists only articles with `category: installation`\n\n**/blog?featured=true**\n- Shows only featured articles (sorted newest first)\n\nBlog index automatically sorts:\n1. Featured articles (by date, newest first)\n2. All other articles (by date, newest first)\n\n---\n\n## How to Add a New Article\n\n### Step 1: Create the MDX file\n\n```bash\ntouch apps/web/content/articles/my-article-slug.mdx\n```\n\n### Step 2: Add frontmatter + content\n\n```yaml\n---\ntitle: My Article Title\ndescription: Short description (max 160 chars for SEO)\nauthor: Mark Carelli\nauthor-title: Lead Architect\npublished-at: 2026-08-05\nmodified-at: null\ncategory: hardwood-science\ntags:\n  - moisture\n  - toronto\nkeywords: \"keyword1, keyword2, keyword3\"\nsemantic-density: 8\ntopics:\n  - Moisture\n  - Toronto Climate\nrelated-articles:\n  - subfloor-moisture-testing-protocol\nfeatured: false\npublished: true\n---\n\n# My Article Title\n\nArticle content in Markdown...\n```\n\n### Step 3: Commit and push\n\n```bash\ngit add apps/web/content/articles/my-article-slug.mdx\ngit commit -m \"content: add article on [topic]\"\ngit push origin main\n```\n\n### Step 4: Deploy (automatic)\n\nVercel auto-deploys from main. Your article appears at:\n- `/blog` (blog index lists it)\n- `/blog/my-article-slug` (article page with auto-injected schema)\n\n**Zero configuration. Zero manual schema setup. Fully automatic.**\n\n---\n\n## Artic