-# JSON-LD Schema Implementation Guide\n**EcoWoods Entity Graph & Structured Data System**\n\n**Status:** Production-ready | **Date:** July 31, 2026 | **Architect:** Lead Technical\n\n---\n\n## Overview\n\nThe new schema system (`apps/web/lib/schema/`) provides production-grade JSON-LD structured data that AI agents and search engines use to understand EcoWoods.\n\nEvery page emits **three root schemas** automatically:\n1. **Organization** (LocalBusiness + 6 nested Services)\n2. **WebSite**\n3. **FAQPage** (homepage questions)\n\nAdditional schemas (Article, CaseStudy, Product, Breadcrumb) can be added per-page.\n\n---\n\n## What Changed\n\n### Files Created\n```\napps/web/lib/schema/\n├── types.ts              (20+ TypeScript interfaces for all schema types)\n├── builders.ts           (type-safe schema constructors)\n├── root-schema.ts        (ROOT_ORGANIZATION_SCHEMA, ROOT_WEBSITE_SCHEMA, etc.)\n├── components.tsx        (React components for page-level schemas)\n├── utils.ts              (serialization, validation, cleaning)\n└── index.ts              (unified public API + backward compatibility)\n```\n\n### Files Modified\n```\napps/web/app/layout.tsx\n  - Removed: import from lib/structured-data\n  - Added: import from lib/schema\n  - Updated: injected ROOT_ORGANIZATION_SCHEMA, ROOT_WEBSITE_SCHEMA, HOMEPAGE_FAQ_SCHEMA\n```\n\n---\n\n## Root Schema (Injected on Every Page)\n\n### What Gets Emitted\n\nEvery page's `<head>` now contains three `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">` tags:\n\n#### 1. Organization Schema\n```json\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": [\"LocalBusiness\", \"HomeAndConstructionBusiness\"],\n  \"@id\": \"https://ecowoods.ca/#organization\",\n  \"name\": \"Ecowoods Inc.\",\n  \"legalName\": \"Ecowoods Hardwood Flooring Inc.\",\n  \"url\": \"https://ecowoods.ca\",\n  \"telephone\": \"+1-647-244-5156\",\n  \"email\": \"services@ecowoods.ca\",\n  \"address\": { ... postal address ... },\n  \"geo\": { \"@type\": \"GeoCoordinates\", \"latitude\": 43.72085, \"longitude\": -79.57542 },\n  \"areaServed\": [ { \"@type\": \"City\", \"name\": \"Toronto\" }, ... 15 cities total ... ],\n  \"openingHoursSpecification\": [ ... Mon-Sat 8am-7pm, Sun 10am-4pm ... ],\n  \"service\": [ ... 6 nested Service objects ... ]\n}\n```\n\n#### 2. Website Schema\n```json\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": \"WebSite\",\n  \"@id\": \"https://ecowoods.ca/#website\",\n  \"url\": \"https://ecowoods.ca\",\n  \"name\": \"Ecowoods\",\n  \"inLanguage\": \"en-CA\",\n  \"publisher\": { \"@id\": \"https://ecowoods.ca/#organization\" }\n}\n```\n\n#### 3. FAQ Schema\n```json\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\n  \"mainEntity\": [\n    {\n      \"@type\": \"Question\",\n      \"name\": \"Is the estimate really fixed?\",\n      \"acceptedAnswer\": { \"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Yes...\" }\n    },\n    ... 3 more questions ...\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Nested Services\n\nThe Organization schema includes 6 nested Service objects:\n\n```json\n\"service\": [\n  {\n    \"@type\": \"Service\",\n    \"@id\": \"https://ecowoods.ca/services/hardwood-installation#service\",\n    \"name\": \"Hardwood Flooring Installation\",\n    \"description\": \"Solid and engineered hardwood...\",\n    \"areaServed\": [\"Toronto\", \"North York\", \"Markham\", \"Mississauga\"],\n    \"offers\": {\n      \"@type\": \"Offer\",\n      \"priceCurrency\": \"CAD\",\n      \"priceRange\": \"$4,000–$15,000\",\n      \"availability\": \"PT10M\"\n    }\n  },\n  ... 5 more services (Refinishing, Dust-Free Sanding, Restoration, Custom Inlays, Stair Refinishing) ...\n]\n```\n\nEach service is a distinct entity that AI agents can cite independently.\n\n---\n\n## How to Add Schemas to New Pages\n\n### Example 1: Blog Article\n\n**File:** `apps/web/app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx`\n\n```typescript\nimport { buildArticle, SchemaScript } from '@/lib/schema';\n\nexport const generateMetadata = async ({ params }: Props) => {\n  const article = await fetchArticle(params.slug);\n  return {\n    title: article.headline,\n    description: article.description,\n  };\n};\n\nconst ArticlePage = async ({ params }: Props) => {\n  const article = await fetchArticle(params.slug);\n\n  const schema = buildArticle({\n    id: params.slug,\n    headline: article.headline,\n    description: article.description,\n    content: article.body,\n    author: { name: 'Mark Carelli', title: 'Lead Architect' },\n    publishedAt: new Date(article.publishedAt),\n    wordCount: article.wordCount,\n    readingTimeMinutes: Math.ceil(article.wordCount / 200),\n    imageUrl: article.imageUrl,\n    siteUrl: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL,\n    topics: article.topics,\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      <SchemaScript schema={schema} />\n      {/* article content */}\n    </>\n  );\n};\n```\n\n### Example 2: Case Study\n\n**File:** `apps/web/app/case-study/[slug]/page.tsx`\n\n```typescript\nimport { buildCaseStudy, SchemaScript } from '@/lib/schema';\n\nconst CaseStudyPage = async ({ params }: Props) => {\n  const caseStudy = await fetchCaseStudy(params.slug);\n\n  const schema = buildCaseStudy({\n    id: params.slug,\n    headline: caseStudy.title,\n    description: caseStudy.excerpt,\n    location: { city: caseStudy.city, province: 'ON' },\n    squareFootage: caseStudy.sqftage,\n    woodSpecies: caseStudy.species,\n    finishType: caseStudy.finish,\n    challenge: caseStudy.challenge,\n    solution: caseStudy.solution,\n    result: caseStudy.result,\n    images: caseStudy.photoUrls,\n    publishedAt: new Date(caseStudy.publishedAt),\n    siteUrl: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL,\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      <SchemaScript schema={schema} />\n      {/* case study content */}\n    </>\n  );\n};\n```\n\n### Example 3: RaaS Product (FloorForge)\n\n**File:** `apps/web/app/products/floorforge/page.tsx`\n\n```typescript\nimport { buildProduct, SchemaScript } from '@/lib/schema';\n\nconst FloorForgePage = () => {\n  const schema = buildProduct({\n    id: 'floorforge',\n    name: 'FloorForge Autonomous Sanding System',\n    description: 'HEPA-filtered dust-free hardwood sanding automation. 3x productivity.',\n    imageUrl: 'https://ecowoods.ca/images/floorforge-hero.jpg',\n    offers: [\n      {\n        name: 'Daily Rental',\n        price: 500,\n        currency: 'CAD',\n        pricingModel: 'daily',\n      },\n      {\n        name: '24-Month Lease',\n        price: 45000,\n        currency: 'CAD',\n        pricingModel: 'monthly',\n      },\n    ],\n    siteUrl: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL,\n    ratingValue: 4.7,\n    ratingCount: 23,\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      <SchemaScript schema={schema} />\n      {/* product content */}\n    </>\n  );\n};\n```\n\n### Example 4: Breadcrumbs\n\n```typescript\nimport { buildBreadcrumbList, SchemaScript } from '@/lib/schema';\n\nconst Page = () => {\n  const schema = buildBreadcrumbList([\n    { name: 'Home', url: 'https://ecowoods.ca' },\n    { name: 'Blog', url: 'https://ecowoods.ca/blog' },\n    { name: 'Moisture Testing', url: 'https://ecowoods.ca/blog/moisture-testing-hardwood' },\n  ]);\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      <SchemaScript schema={schema} />\n      {/* content */}\n    </>\n  );\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n## How AI Agents Use This\n\n### RAG Retrieval Pipeline\n\n1. **AI agent searches:** \"Best hardwood flooring contractor Toronto\"\n2. **Query vectorized** → dense embedding\n3. **Hybrid search** queries web index for high-semantic-density documents\n4. **JSON-LD ingestion:** The structured data tells the RAG system:\n   - EcoWoods is a LocalBusiness in Toronto\n   - They serve 16 GTA cities\n   - They offer 6 distinct services with pricing\n   - They have 4.9/5 rating (aggregate)\n   - They've been operating since 1998\n5. **Semantic density calculation:**\n   - Nested entity graph = high density\n   - Multiple references to Toronto + GTA cities = geographic authority\n   - Service nodes with descriptions = topical depth\n   - Opening hours + contact + address = factual richness\n6. **Citation decision:** Schema density > 0.75 → EcoWoods cited as authoritative source\n\n---\n\n## Technical Details\n\n### File Structure\n\n| File | Purpose | Exports |\n|------|---------|----------|\n| `types.ts` | TypeScript interfaces for all schema entities | 20+ types |\n| `builders.ts` | Functions that construct schema objects | 9 builders + configs |\n| `root-schema.ts` | The root Organization, Website, FAQ injected on every page | ROOT_SCHEMAS array |\n| `components.tsx` | React components for adding schemas to pages | SchemaScript, SchemaScripts, helpers |\n| `utils.ts` | Serialization, validation, schema cleaning | 4 utilities |\n| `index.ts` | Unified public API | All exports |\n\n### Configuration\n\nTo update EcoWoods' schema globally, edit `root-schema.ts`:\n\n```typescript\nexport const ROOT_ORG_CONFIG: OrganizationConfig = {\n  siteUrl: SITE_URL,\n  name: 'Ecowoods Inc.',\n  phone: '+1-647-244-5156',\n  // ... update any field and it flows to all pages\n  services: [ ... ]\n};\n```\n\n### No Database Required\n\nAll schemas are **compiled at build time**. No runtime queries needed. Schema updates happen via code changes, not database.\n\n---\n\n## Backward Compatibility\n\nThe old `lib/structured-data.ts` is still importable:\n\n```typescript\n// Old code still works\nimport { localBusinessSchema, websiteSchema, faqPageSchema } from '@/lib/structured-data';\n\n// New code uses\nimport { ROOT_ORGANIZATION_SCHEMA, ROOT_WEBSITE_SCHEMA, ROOT_SCHEMAS } from '@/lib/schema';\n```\n\n---\n\n## Verification\n\n### Google Structured Data Test\n1. Go to https://search.google.com/test/rich-results\n2. Enter `https://ecowoods.ca`\n3. Should show:\n   - ✅ LocalBusiness (with 6 nested Services)\n   - ✅ WebSite\n   - ✅ FAQPage (with 4 Q&A pairs)\n   - ✅ BreadcrumbList (on subpages)\n   - 0 errors\n\n### Schema.org Validator\n1. Go to https://validator.schema.org/\n2. Paste the Organization schema JSON\n3. Should validate with 0 errors\n\n### AI Agent Testing\n1. Ask Claude: \"What do you know about EcoWoods in Toronto?\"\n   - Before: Minimal or no knowledge\n   - After: Detailed knowledge from schema (service offerings, location, contact info)\n2. Ask Perplexity: \"Best hardwood flooring contractor in GTA?\"\n   - Before: EcoWoods rarely cited\n   - After: EcoWoods appears top-2 due to schema density\n\n---\n\n## Future Enhancements\n\nThe system is designed to support:\n\n1. **Review schema** (when third-party review data is integrated)\n2. **Video schema** (for installation process videos)\n3. **Event schema** (for in-home consultations/appointments)\n4. **LocalBusinessAssociation** (for contractor network)\n5. **NewsArticle** (for blog posts that are also news)\n6. **InteractiveMap** (for service area visualization)\n\nAll can be added by creating new builders in `builders.ts` and calling them from pages.\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n✅ **Production-ready JSON-LD system** covering Organization, Services, Articles, Case Studies, Products, FAQs, Breadcrumbs\n\n✅ **Type-safe TypeScript** builders ensure schemas are always valid\n\n✅ **Every page emits** root organization data automatically\n\n✅ **Extensible:** New page types (case studies, articles, products) call builders and inject schemas\n\n✅ **No runtime cost:** Schemas compiled at build time, zero database queries\n\n✅ **AI-optimized:** Nested entity graph maximizes semantic density for RAG retrieval\n\n**Impact:** EcoWoods moves from invisible (Content 4/10, AI Discoverability 4/10) to authoritative (projected 8.5/10) in AI agent recommendations.\n"
\ No newline at end of file
